.5453], [1.275, 3.5787], [1.2844, 3.6124], [1.2937, 3.6464], [1.3031, 3.6808], [1.3125, 3.7155], [1.3219, 3.7504], [1.3313, 3.7858], [1.3406, 3.8214], [1.35, 3.8574], [1.3594, 3.8938], [1.3687, 3.9304], [1.3781, 3.9675], [1.3875, 4.0048], [1.3969, 4.0425], [1.4062, 4.0806], [1.4156, 4.1191], [1.425, 4.1579], [1.4344, 4.197], [1.4438, 4.2366], [1.4531, 4.2765], [1.4625, 4.3167], [1.4719, 4.3574], [1.4812, 4.3984], [1.4906, 4.4399], [1.5, 4.4817]], "label": "Exact"}, {"c": 1, "dash": true, "step": 2, "pts": [[0, 1], [0.5, 1.5]]}, {"c": 1, "dash": true, "step": 3, "pts": [[0.5, 1.5], [1, 2.25]]}, {"c": 1, "dash": true, "label": "Euler, h = 0.5", "step": 4, "pts": [[1, 2.25], [1.5, 3.375]]}, {"c": 2, "label": "Euler, h = 0.25", "step": 5, "pts": [[0, 1], [0.25, 1.25], [0.5, 1.5625], [0.75, 1.953125], [1, 2.44140625], [1.25, 3.0517578], [1.5, 3.8146973]]}], "points": [{"at": [0, 1], "label": "start"}, {"at": [0.5, 1.5], "label": "y₁", "step": 2}, {"at": [1, 2.25], "label": "y₂", "step": 3}, {"at": [1.5, 3.375], "label": "y₃", "step": 4}], "steps": ["The exact solution of dy/dx = y with y = 1 at x = 0 is y = eˣ. Euler's method will try to follow this curve from the start point.", "At (0, 1) the gradient is y = 1. Move h = 0.5 along it: y₁ = 1 + 0.5 × 1 = 1.5 at x = 0.5. The line already falls below the curve.", "At (0.5, 1.5) the gradient is 1.5. Step on: y₂ = 1.5 + 0.5 × 1.5 = 2.25 at x = 1. The gap to the exact curve is growing.", "At (1, 2.25) the gradient is 2.25: y₃ = 2.25 + 0.5 × 2.25 = 3.375 at x = 1.5. The exact value is 4.48, so the error has built up.", "Halving the step length to h = 0.25 gives 3.81 at x = 1.5 (3 s.f.), much closer to 4.48. A smaller h usually gives a better estimate."]}}], "example": {"task": "The graph shows $y=\\dfrac1x$ for $1\\le x\\le3$. Use Simpson's rule with 4 strips to estimate $\\int_1^3\\dfrac{1}{x}\\,\\mathrm{d}x$. Give your answer to 3 significant figures.", "steps": [{"do": "Find $h=\\dfrac{3-1}{4}=0.5$. The ordinates are at $x=1,\\,1.5,\\,2,\\,2.5,\\,3$.", "why": "Strip width is $(b-a)/n$. Four strips need five ordinates."}, {"do": "Evaluate $y=1/x$: $y_0=1$, $y_1=\\tfrac23$, $y_2=\\tfrac12$, $y_3=\\tfrac25$, $y_4=\\tfrac13$.", "why": "Keeping exact fractions avoids rounding errors building up."}, {"do": "Write $\\dfrac{h}{3}\\left[y_0+y_4+4(y_1+y_3)+2y_2\\right]$.", "why": "Ends have weight 1, odd ordinates 4, the middle (even) ordinate 2."}, {"do": "Substitute: $\\dfrac{0.5}{3}\\left[1+\\tfrac13+4\\left(\\tfrac23+\\tfrac25\\right)+2\\left(\\tfrac12\\right)\\right]=\\dfrac16\\left[\\tfrac43+\\tfrac{64}{15}+1\\right]$.", "why": "Shows the formula with correct values, which earns the method mark."}, {"do": "Simplify: $\\dfrac16\\times\\dfrac{99}{15}=\\dfrac16\\times6.6=1.1$.", "why": "$\\tfrac{20}{15}+\\tfrac{64}{15}+\\tfrac{15}{15}=\\tfrac{99}{15}$, and $\\tfrac{99}{15}=6.6$."}], "answer": "$\\int_1^3\\frac1x\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\approx1.10$ (3 s.f.). The exact value is $\\ln 3\\approx1.0986$, so the estimate is very close.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "x": [1, 3], "y": [0, 1.2], "xstep": 0.5, "ystep": 0.2, "xlabel": "x", "ylabel": "y", "lines": [{"pts": [[1.0, 1.0], [1.0125, 0.987654], [1.025, 0.97561], [1.0375, 0.963855], [1.05, 0.952381], [1.0625, 0.941176], [1.075, 0.930233], [1.0875, 0.91954], [1.1, 0.909091], [1.1125, 0.898876], [1.125, 0.888889], [1.1375, 0.879121], [1.15, 0.869565], [1.1625, 0.860215], [1.175, 0.851064], [1.1875, 0.842105], [1.2, 0.833333], [1.2125, 0.824742], [1.225, 0.816327], [1.2375, 0.808081], [1.25, 0.8], [1.2625, 0.792079], [1.275, 0.784314], [1.2875, 0.776699], [1.3, 0.769231], [1.3125, 0.761905], [1.325, 0.754717], [1.3375, 0.747664], [1.35, 0.740741], [1.3625, 0.733945], [1.375, 0.727273], [1.3875, 0.720721], [1.4, 0.714286], [1.4125, 0.707965], [1.425, 0.701754], [1.4375, 0.695652], [1.45, 0.689655], [1.4625, 0.683761], [1.475, 0.677966], [1.4875, 0.672269], [1.5, 0.666667], [1.5125, 0.661157], [1.525, 0.655738], [1.5375, 0.650407], [1.55, 0.645161], [1.5625, 0.64], [1.575, 0.634921], [1.5875, 0.629921], [1.6, 0.625], [1.6125, 0.620155], [1.625, 0.615385], [1.6375, 0.610687], [1.65, 0.606061], [1.6625, 0.601504], [1.675, 0.597015], [1.6875, 0.592593], [1.7, 0.588235], [1.7125, 0.583942], [1.725, 0.57971], [1.7375, 0.57554], [1.75, 0.571429], [1.7625, 0.567376], [1.775, 0.56338], [1.7875, 0.559441], [1.8, 0.555556], [1.8125, 0.551724], [1.825, 0.547945], [1.8375, 0.544218], [1.85, 0.540541], [1.8625, 0.536913], [1.875, 0.533333], [1.8875, 0.529801], [1.9, 0.526316], [1.9125, 0.522876], [1.925, 0.519481], [1.9375, 0.516129], [1.95, 0.512821], [1.9625, 0.509554], [1.975, 0.506329], [1.9875, 0.503145], [2.0, 0.5], [2.0125, 0.496894], [2.025, 0.493827], [2.0375, 0.490798], [2.05, 0.487805], [2.0625, 0.484848], [2.075, 0.481928], [2.0875, 0.479042], [2.1, 0.47619], [2.1125, 0.473373], [2.125, 0.470588], [2.1375, 0.467836], [2.15, 0.465116], [2.1625, 0.462428], [2.175, 0.45977], [2.1875, 0.457143], [2.2, 0.454545], [2.2125, 0.451977], [2.225, 0.449438], [2.2375, 0.446927], [2.25, 0.444444], [2.2625, 0.441989], [2.275, 0.43956], [2.2875, 0.437158], [2.3, 0.434783], [2.3125, 0.432432], [2.325, 0.430108], [2.3375, 0.427807], [2.35, 0.425532], [2.3625, 0.42328], [2.375, 0.421053], [2.3875, 0.418848], [2.4, 0.416667], [2.4125, 0.414508], [2.425, 0.412371], [2.4375, 0.410256], [2.45, 0.408163], [2.4625, 0.406091], [2.475, 0.40404], [2.4875, 0.40201], [2.5, 0.4], [2.5125, 0.39801], [2.525, 0.39604], [2.5375, 0.394089], [2.55, 0.392157], [2.5625, 0.390244], [2.575, 0.38835], [2.5875, 0.386473], [2.6, 0.384615], [2.6125, 0.382775], [2.625, 0.380952], [2.6375, 0.379147], [2.65, 0.377358], [2.6625, 0.375587], [2.675, 0.373832], [2.6875, 0.372093], [2.7, 0.37037], [2.7125, 0.368664], [2.725, 0.366972], [2.7375, 0.365297], [2.75, 0.363636], [2.7625, 0.361991], [2.775, 0.36036], [2.7875, 0.358744], [2.8, 0.357143], [2.8125, 0.355556], [2.825, 0.353982], [2.8375, 0.352423], [2.85, 0.350877], [2.8625, 0.349345], [2.875, 0.347826], [2.8875, 0.34632], [2.9, 0.344828], [2.9125, 0.343348], [2.925, 0.34188], [2.9375, 0.340426], [2.95, 0.338983], [2.9625, 0.337553], [2.975, 0.336134], [2.9875, 0.334728], [3.0, 0.333333]], "c": 0}]}}, "selfx": {"q": "Why could this question not have used Simpson's rule with 3 strips?", "o": ["Three strips give $h=\\tfrac23$, which is a recurring decimal and so not allowed.", "Three strips give four ordinates, which is too few for the formula to work.", "Simpson's rule fits a parabola over each pair of strips, so $n$ must be even.", "The function $1/x$ cannot be integrated numerically over an odd number of strips."], "a": 2, "f": ["Wrong: $h$ can be any width, including a recurring decimal. The restriction is on the number of strips, not on $h$.", "Wrong: the formula has no minimum of five ordinates. The real issue is that strips must pair up, not how many ordinates there are.", "Right: each parabola spans two strips, so the strips must pair up. That is why $n$ must be even.", "Wrong: the type of function does not matter. The even-$n$ rule applies to any integrand."]}, "faded": {"task": "$\\dfrac{\\mathrm{d}y}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2x-y$, $y=3$ when $x=1$. Use Euler's method with $h=0.2$ to estimate $y$ when $x=1.4$.", "given": ["$x_0=1,\\ y_0=3,\\ h=0.2$", "$y_1=3+0.2(2\\times1-3)=2.8$, at $x_1=1.2$"], "q": "What is the next step, and the estimate of $y$ at $x=1.4$?", "o": ["$y_2=2.8+0.2(2\\times1.4-2.8)=2.8$", "$y_2=2.8+0.2(2\\times1.2-2.8)=2.72$", "$y_2=2.8+0.2(2\\times1.2-3)=2.68$", "$y_2=2.8+(2\\times1.2-2.8)=2.4$"], "a": 1, "f": ["Wrong: this puts the new value $x=1.4$ into the gradient. Euler uses the start of the step, $x_1=1.2$.", "Right: the gradient is evaluated at $(x_1,y_1)=(1.2,\\,2.8)$, giving $-0.4$, then multiplied by $h=0.2$ and added to 2.8.", "Wrong: this reuses the old $y_0=3$ in the gradient. Each step must use the latest $y$, here $y_1=2.8$.", "Wrong: this leaves out the factor $h$. The increment is $h\\,f(x_r,y_r)$, not just $f(x_r,y_r)$."]}, "trap": "In Euler's method, putting the new $x$ or $y$ into $f$. The gradient always comes from the start of the step, $(x_r,y_r)$. In Simpson's rule, keep the 4s on odd ordinates and the 2s on even ones.", "recap": "Simpson's needs an even number of strips, with weights $1,4,2,\\dots,4,1$; Euler's gradient always comes from the start of each step."}
{"s": "further", "t": "fp-polar", "kind": "method", "why": "Polar questions in Core pure papers ask you to convert, sketch and find areas, and the area part usually needs a double-angle identity.", "hook": null, "chunks": [{"h": "Converting between forms", "b": "Use $x=r\\cos\\theta$, $y=r\\sin\\theta$ and $r^2=x^2+y^2$. To find $\\theta$ from $(x,y)$, use $\\tan\\theta=\\frac{y}{x}$, then check the **quadrant**. To convert a polar equation, multiply by $r$ if needed so that $r\\cos\\theta$ or $r\\sin\\theta$ appears. Write points as **$(r,\\theta)$**."}, {"h": "Sketching polar curves", "b": "$r$ is the distance from the **pole**, measured along the direction $\\theta$ from the **initial line**. Press Play: the graph shows $r=2(1+\\cos\\theta)$, and a is $\\theta$. Find the greatest and least $r$ from the trig range, find where $r=0$, and check **symmetry**. If $r<0$, the point lies in the opposite direction.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "anim": "frames", "ms": 200, "x": [-1, 5], "xstep": 1, "y": [-3, 3], "ystep": 1, "xlabel": "x", "ylabel": "y", "equal": true, "lines": [{"c": 2, "pts": [[0, 0], [5, 0]]}, {"dash": true, "c": 3, "pts": [[4.0, 0.0], [3.9954, 0.157], [3.9815, 0.3134], [3.9585, 0.4685], [3.9264, 0.6219], [3.8855, 0.7729], [3.8357, 0.9209], [3.7776, 1.0654], [3.7111, 1.2058], [3.6368, 1.3417], [3.5549, 1.4725], [3.4657, 1.5977], [3.3698, 1.717], [3.2675, 1.8299], [3.1593, 1.936], [3.0456, 2.035], [2.9271, 2.1266], [2.8041, 2.2106], [2.6772, 2.2866], [2.5471, 2.3545], [2.4142, 2.4142], [2.2791, 2.4656], [2.1425, 2.5085], [2.0047, 2.543], [1.8666, 2.5691], [1.7285, 2.5868], [1.591, 2.5963], [1.4547, 2.5976], [1.3202, 2.591], [1.1879, 2.5767], [1.0583, 2.5549], [0.9318, 2.5258], [0.809, 2.4899], [0.6902, 2.4474], [0.5759, 2.3987], [0.4663, 2.3443], [0.3618, 2.2844], [0.2627, 2.2196], [0.1692, 2.1503], [0.0816, 2.0769], [0.0, 2.0], [-0.0754, 1.92], [-0.1446, 1.8374], [-0.2074, 1.7527], [-0.2639, 1.6664], [-0.3141, 1.5789], [-0.3579, 1.4907], [-0.3955, 1.4024],