1, "pts": [[-1.0, -1.0], [4.0, 9.0]], "label": "y = 2x + c"}], "read": ["x² = 2x + c gives x² − 2x − c = 0", "b² − 4ac = 4 + 4c = 8", "Tangent when 4 + 4c = 0, so c = −1"]}, {"lines": [{"c": 1, "pts": [[-1.0, -0.5], [4.0, 9.5]], "label": "y = 2x + c"}], "read": ["x² = 2x + c gives x² − 2x − c = 0", "b² − 4ac = 4 + 4c = 10", "Tangent when 4 + 4c = 0, so c = −1"]}, {"lines": [{"c": 1, "pts": [[-1.0, 0.0], [4.0, 10.0]], "label": "y = 2x + c"}], "read": ["x² = 2x + c gives x² − 2x − c = 0", "b² − 4ac = 4 + 4c = 12", "Tangent when 4 + 4c = 0, so c = −1"]}], "ctl": {"type": "slider", "label": "c", "vals": ["−3", "−2.5", "−2", "−1.5", "−1", "−0.5", "0", "0.5", "1", "1.5", "2"], "start": 10}}}], "example": {"task": "Solve $15-2x-x^2>0$. The graph shows $y=x^2+2x-15$, the expression you get after multiplying through by $-1$, with its roots marked.", "steps": [{"do": "Multiply both sides by $-1$ and reverse the sign: $x^2+2x-15<0$.", "why": "This makes the $x^2$ term positive, so the graph is U-shaped. Multiplying by a negative reverses the inequality."}, {"do": "Solve $x^2+2x-15=0$: $(x+5)(x-3)=0$, so $x=-5$ or $x=3$.", "why": "The roots are where the curve meets the $x$-axis, so they are the boundaries of the solution."}, {"do": "Sketch a U-shaped curve crossing the $x$-axis at $-5$ and $3$.", "why": "The sketch shows where the curve is above or below the axis. No exact plotting is needed."}, {"do": "Read off where the curve is below the axis, as $x^2+2x-15<0$ asks. That is between the roots.", "why": "A U-shaped curve is negative between its roots. The inequality is strict, so the roots are excluded."}], "answer": "$-5<x<3$. Check with $x=0$: $15-0-0=15>0$, which is true.", "fig": {"type": "graph", "x": [-6, 3], "y": [-16, 12], "xstep": 1, "ystep": 4, "xlabel": "x", "ylabel": "y", "lines": [{"pts": [[-6.0, 9.0], [-5.94375, 8.440664], [-5.8875, 7.887656], [-5.83125, 7.340977], [-5.775, 6.800625], [-5.71875, 6.266602], [-5.6625, 5.738906], [-5.60625, 5.217539], [-5.55, 4.7025], [-5.49375, 4.193789], [-5.4375, 3.691406], [-5.38125, 3.195352], [-5.325, 2.705625], [-5.26875, 2.222227], [-5.2125, 1.745156], [-5.15625, 1.274414], [-5.1, 0.81], [-5.04375, 0.351914], [-4.9875, -0.099844], [-4.93125, -0.545273], [-4.875, -0.984375], [-4.81875, -1.417148], [-4.7625, -1.843594], [-4.70625, -2.263711], [-4.65, -2.6775], [-4.59375, -3.084961], [-4.5375, -3.486094], [-4.48125, -3.880898], [-4.425, -4.269375], [-4.36875, -4.651523], [-4.3125, -5.027344], [-4.25625, -5.396836], [-4.2, -5.76], [-4.14375, -6.116836], [-4.0875, -6.467344], [-4.03125, -6.811523], [-3.975, -7.149375], [-3.91875, -7.480898], [-3.8625, -7.806094], [-3.80625, -8.124961], [-3.75, -8.4375], [-3.69375, -8.743711], [-3.6375, -9.043594], [-3.58125, -9.337148], [-3.525, -9.624375], [-3.46875, -9.905273], [-3.4125, -10.179844], [-3.35625, -10.448086], [-3.3, -10.71], [-3.24375, -10.965586], [-3.1875, -11.214844], [-3.13125, -11.457773], [-3.075, -11.694375], [-3.01875, -11.924648], [-2.9625, -12.148594], [-2.90625, -12.366211], [-2.85, -12.5775], [-2.79375, -12.782461], [-2.7375, -12.981094], [-2.68125, -13.173398], [-2.625, -13.359375], [-2.56875, -13.539023], [-2.5125, -13.712344], [-2.45625, -13.879336], [-2.4, -14.04], [-2.34375, -14.194336], [-2.2875, -14.342344], [-2.23125, -14.484023], [-2.175, -14.619375], [-2.11875, -14.748398], [-2.0625, -14.871094], [-2.00625, -14.987461], [-1.95, -15.0975], [-1.89375, -15.201211], [-1.8375, -15.298594], [-1.78125, -15.389648], [-1.725, -15.474375], [-1.66875, -15.552773], [-1.6125, -15.624844], [-1.55625, -15.690586], [-1.5, -15.75], [-1.44375, -15.803086], [-1.3875, -15.849844], [-1.33125, -15.890273], [-1.275, -15.924375], [-1.21875, -15.952148], [-1.1625, -15.973594], [-1.10625, -15.988711], [-1.05, -15.9975], [-0.99375, -15.999961], [-0.9375, -15.996094], [-0.88125, -15.985898], [-0.825, -15.969375], [-0.76875, -15.946523], [-0.7125, -15.917344], [-0.65625, -15.881836], [-0.6, -15.84], [-0.54375, -15.791836], [-0.4875, -15.737344], [-0.43125, -15.676523], [-0.375, -15.609375], [-0.31875, -15.535898], [-0.2625, -15.456094], [-0.20625, -15.369961], [-0.15, -15.2775], [-0.09375, -15.178711], [-0.0375, -15.073594], [0.01875, -14.962148], [0.075, -14.844375], [0.13125, -14.720273], [0.1875, -14.589844], [0.24375, -14.453086], [0.3, -14.31], [0.35625, -14.160586], [0.4125, -14.004844], [0.46875, -13.842773], [0.525, -13.674375], [0.58125, -13.499648], [0.6375, -13.318594], [0.69375, -13.131211], [0.75, -12.9375], [0.80625, -12.737461], [0.8625, -12.531094], [0.91875, -12.318398], [0.975, -12.099375], [1.03125, -11.874023], [1.0875, -11.642344], [1.14375, -11.404336], [1.2, -11.16], [1.25625, -10.909336], [1.3125, -10.652344], [1.36875, -10.389023], [1.425, -10.119375], [1.48125, -9.843398], [1.5375, -9.561094], [1.59375, -9.272461], [1.65, -8.9775], [1.70625, -8.676211], [1.7625, -8.368594], [1.81875, -8.054648], [1.875, -7.734375], [1.93125, -7.407773], [1.9875, -7.074844], [2.04375, -6.735586], [2.1, -6.39], [2.15625, -6.038086], [2.2125, -5.679844], [2.26875, -5.315273], [2.325, -4.944375], [2.38125, -4.567148], [2.4375, -4.183594], [2.49375, -3.793711], [2.55, -3.3975], [2.60625, -2.994961], [2.6625, -2.586094], [2.71875, -2.170898], [2.775, -1.749375], [2.83125, -1.321523], [2.8875, -0.887344], [2.94375, -0.446836], [3.0, 0.0]], "c": 0, "label": "y=x²+2x-15"}], "points": [{"at": [-5, 0], "label": "-5"}, {"at": [3, 0], "label": "3"}]}}, "selfx": {"q": "Why does the first step change $>$ into $<$?", "o": ["Because the roots of the quadratic turn out to be negative", "Multiplying by $-1$ reverses the order of numbers, so the sign flips", "Because a U-shaped graph always needs a $<$ sign to be sketched", "Because $x^2$ terms must always be moved to the left-hand side"], "a": 1, "f": ["The sign of the roots has no effect on the inequality sign. The reversal comes only from multiplying by a negative number.", "Right. For example $5>3$ but $-5<-3$. Multiplying by $-1$ flips the order, so the sign must reverse to stay true.", "Sketching does not decide the sign. You choose $<$ or $>$ from the inequality itself, and only afterwards read the sketch.", "Moving terms is a separate step and does not change the sign. Here the reversal is caused by multiplying through by $-1$."]}, "faded": {"task": "Solve $10+3x-x^2<0$.", "given": ["Multiply by $-1$ and reverse the sign: $x^2-3x-10>0$.", "Factorise: $(x-5)(x+2)>0$, so the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=5$."], "q": "What is the next step, and what is the solution?", "o": ["$-2<x<5$, because the curve is between the roots", "$x<-5$ or $x>2$, taking the roots from the bracket numbers", "$x<-2$ or $x>5$, because the U-shaped curve is above the axis there", "$x<-2$ and $x>5$, because both outer regions are needed"], "a": 2, "f": ["This is the region for $<0$. The inequality is now $>0$, which means above the axis, so the outside regions are needed.", "The roots have the opposite signs to the bracket numbers. Set each bracket to zero: $x+2=0$ gives $x=-2$, and $x-5=0$ gives $x=5$.", "Right. The curve is U-shaped and $>0$ means above the axis, so it is outside the roots: $x<-2$ or $x>5$.", "The region is correct but the word is wrong. No number is both below $-2$ and above $5$, so you must write 'or'."]}, "trap": "Forgetting to reverse the sign when multiplying or dividing by a negative. Whenever you multiply through by $-1$ to make $x^2$ positive, flip the sign, then test one value from your answer.", "recap": "Make $x^2$ positive, find the roots, sketch the U: $>0$ is outside the roots, $<0$ is between them."}
